WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.709
Bad Bunny is a trap
rapper who is making waves

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.244
in the Latin music world.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.481
His debut album, "X 100PRE,"
scored the No. 1 spot

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.117
on the Top Latin Albums chart this year.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.619
But it's probably not the
first time you've seen him.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.488
He's worked with Cardi B on "I Like It"

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.922
and "Mia" with Drake.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.058
And he just dropped his
new song, "Callaita."

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.794
But Bad Bunny's appeal extends beyond

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.430
these star-studded music collaborations.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.565
He's been instrumental
in bringing Latin trap

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.701
to mainstream American audiences

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.636
while rapping mostly in Spanish.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.438
Bad Bunny originally posted his music

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.140
on SoundCloud independently

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.610
but was quickly noticed and
signed on to a record label.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.712
Since then, he's been a
consistent heavy hitter

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.147
on the Hot Latin Songs chart,

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.717
with 46 tracks, and seven on the Hot 100.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.752
Along with his own singles, he's teamed up

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.121
with other Hispanic and Latino top artists

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.556
to create Billboard hits,

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.559
such as "Sensualidad" with
J Balvin and Prince Royce,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.996
and a remix of "Te Bote"
with Ozuna and Nicky Jam.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:06.199
In 2018, he collaborated
with Cardi B and J Balvin

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.400
for "I Like It,"

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.803
making it Bad Bunny's first No. 1 single

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.471
on the US Billboards.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.239
It was followed with another collaboration

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.609
with Drake for "Mia," and
Jennifer Lopez for "Te Guste,"

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.446
garnering him even more fans in the US

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.980
and around the world.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.516
This leads up to his
debut album, "X 100PRE,"

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.519
which, unsurprisingly,
skyrocketed to the No. 1 spot

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.521
on the Top Latin Albums chart.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:31.091
With his rhythmic cadence and slow slurs,

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.526
Bad Bunny has a unique
sound that is unlike

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.728
anything else on the Latin music scene.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.530
This is largely due to his willingness

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.533
to cross music genres,
ranging from Latin trap,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.202
reggaeton, and pop.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.204
In an interview with Billboard, he credits

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.206
his unique music style to his parents

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.274
and home country of Puerto Rico.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.343
When he was little, he listened to salsa,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.278
merengue, and pop ballads.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:56.082
At the same time, he was singing
to reggaeton and hip hop.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.884
Bad Bunny's rise to fame isn't only

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.285
attributed to his music,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.521
but to his unshakeable sense of self.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.723
He has a distinct style,
with his painted nails

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.558
and bright patterns, which have made him

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.327
a fashion inspiration.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.428
And you're likely to spot him

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.863
with a pair of trendy shades.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.600
In a music culture that often champions

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.003
traditional masculinity, Bad
Bunny is a breath of fresh air

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:20.640
that redefines gender norms
and societal expectations.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.509
Through his music and clothing choices,

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:26.045
he preaches messages of
self-love and respect for others.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.580
In the music video for "Caro,"

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.682
there are several gender-bending moments,

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.652
and even a scene featuring
an inclusive fashion show,

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:36.923
with models of varying ages,
abilities, races, and sizes.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.392
In another music video for "Solo De Mi,"

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.896
he tackles the issue of
domestic violence against women.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:45.064
With just three years
in the music industry

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.800
under his belt, Bad Bunny
has become one of the most

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.903
recognizable faces of Latin trap

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:53.072
while also helping bring
Latin music to the mainstream.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:57.877
In 2018, Bad Bunny was YouTube's
third-most-viewed artist,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.180
with 7 billion views.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.383
Now, Bad Bunny is headlining
his own international tour

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.885
and selling out venues across the world.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.420
He sold out his homecoming concerts

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.522
in Puerto Rico within hours,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.457
which led to adding a third day.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.560
In addition, J Balvin has teased

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.461
an upcoming collaborative album.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.363
Whatever the next album may be,

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.899
we can't wait to see more from Bad Bunny.

